{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.SemistandardTableau","lean:module:Mathlib.SetTheory.Cardinal.Finite"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.numStandardYoungTableaux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.numStandardYoungTableaux","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L102-L107","doc":"**`#SYT(μ)`** — the number of standard Young tableaux of shape `μ`, as `Nat.card` (total; no\n`Fintype` instance required to define it).  This is the combinatorial dimension `dim(μ)` whose\nsquare-sum is `n!` (RSK) and whose hook-length closed form is `n!/∏h_c` — both tracked as the\nnext infra steps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.instFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.instFinite","kind":"instance","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L97-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.encode_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.encode_injective","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L85-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.encode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.encode","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L78-L83","doc":"Encode a standard tableau by its (bounded) entries on the cells — the values lie in\n`{1,…,|μ|} ⊆ Fin (|μ|+1)`, and a tableau is determined by them (off-cell entries are `0`).  This\ninjection into a finite function type witnesses finiteness of `StandardYoungTableau μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.row_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.row_strict","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L66-L76","doc":"**Rows are strictly increasing** — not merely weakly, as for a general semistandard tableau.\nOn a row, the SSYT weak-row inequality together with injectivity of the (bijective) filling forces\nstrictness.  This certifies the type is the genuine standard-tableau notion, not a vacuous wrapper. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.mem_coe_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.mem_coe_cells","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L61-L64","doc":"Membership of a cell `(i, j) ∈ μ` as a `Set`-membership in `↑μ.cells` (the form `InjOn`\nconsumes). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.mapsTo_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.mapsTo_cells","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L55-L59","doc":"The entry map sends the cells onto `{1, …, |μ|}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.injOn_cells","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.injOn_cells","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L50-L53","doc":"The entry map is injective on the cells of `μ` (the filling is a bijection). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.entry","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.entry","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L47-L48","doc":"Entry `(i, j)` of a standard Young tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.bijOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.bijOn","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The entry map is a bijection from the cells onto `{1, …, |μ|}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.toSsyt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.toSsyt","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The underlying semistandard tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau.mk","kind":"ctor","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.StandardYoungTableau","kind":"structure","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/StandardYoungTableau.lean#L33-L41","doc":"A **standard Young tableau** of shape `μ`: a semistandard tableau whose entry map restricted to\nthe cells of `μ` is a bijection onto `{1, …, |μ|}`.  (Strict rows follow from weak rows +\ninjectivity — see `StandardYoungTableau.row_strict`.) ","signatureChunk":0}]}